messages:
maya: Quick design heads-up — on tiny viewports (iPhone SE / 320px) the left rail sometimes overlays the first couple table rows when the rail is expanded. Screenshot: https://img.redwood/mock/rail-overlap.png

nate: Can repro locally, thanks. Is this only when the rail is forced open, or also when it auto-collapses?

maya: Forced open — we have the rail pinned on some workspaces for quick nav. At <=360px it sits on top of the table instead of pushing content. At 420px it still pushes, so looks like a breakpoint mismatch.

sophia: From a product POV primary content (table rows) should never be occluded. Options: auto-collapse rail under X px, convert table to a stacked list/cards, or make rail overlay with a visible dismiss affordance. Thoughts?

kevin: Accessibility nit — when the rail overlays it hides focusable row actions. Keyboard users can’t reach those items and screen reader users get confused because visual focus and DOM order differ. We need aria-hidden toggles and ensure focus is moved to a logical element after toggle. Also contrast for the pinned toggle is below 4.5:1 on the gray variant.

nate: Agreed. Quick implementation plan: 1) add CSS breakpoint at 400px to auto-collapse the rail, 2) add an overlay mode with a scrim and focus trap if user explicitly opens it, 3) switch tables to stacked cards at <=360px to avoid horizontal scrolling. Prototype CSS sketch:

```css
/* prototype */
@media (max-width: 400px) {
  .console-rail { transform: translateX(-100%); /* collapsed by default */ }
  .console-rail.open { position: fixed; right: 0; left: auto; z-index: 800; }
  .main-content { padding-left: 0; }
}
.table-container { overflow-x: auto; -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch; }
```

maya: That looks reasonable. Two small follow-ups: ensure header columns stay aligned when switching modes, and preserve the table sort/filter controls (maybe move them above the stacked cards).

sophia: If we move to stacked cards we should keep copy consistent — row summary heading, timestamp, and the primary action button. UX copy tweak: use "View details" instead of "Expand" for clarity on small screens.

kevin: Add to checklist: 1) keyboard focus after rail open/close, 2) aria-hidden for covered content, 3) scrim has role="dialog" semantics when rail is in overlay mode, 4) button contrast >= 4.5:1.

nate: I'll do a small prototype branch and include a Percy snapshot and axe run. Will also add an E2E that tabs through rail toggle -> first row action. Estimated PR by EOD Friday.

maya: Awesome — please tag me and add screenshots of both 360px and 420px states. Also add a short note in the component README about the auto-collapse behaviour.

design-bot: Added to the design review agenda for Thu 10:00am. :spiral_calendar_pad:

sophia: Thanks team — this should unblock the mobile dashboard bug. :thumbsup:
